  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Right on the harbour of Nice, La Barque Bleue has served fish (grilled, baked, in sauce) and Niçois specialities facing the moored boats since 1982, alongside fresh Italian-style pasta — mussels marinière and vongole linguine are especially popular.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The official Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office page states that the establishment "has always spontaneously welcomed four-legged friends and, thanks to the Pet Friendly label, it's now official." A local press article (NicePresse) also confirms that the restaurant is among the Pet Friendly-labelled addresses at the harbour of Nice.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the quay makes for a lovely walk before or after the meal, between the boats and the harbour's colourful façades.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The harbour of Nice and its Belle Époque architecture are easy to explore on foot, with Vieux Nice just a few minutes away.</p>
